    <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Collection"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Root container for cultural heritage data instances. PLACEMENT RULE: put each instance in the most specific collection available (e.g. a Festival in festivals, not ritual_events; a Person in persons, not actors); broader collections exist for instances of the general classes only.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/schema"/>
    <heritageGraph:design_note>Serialization construct, not a domain class: this is the LinkML tree_root that anchors JSON/YAML dataset serializations (its collection properties exist for data exchange only). Reasoners and domain queries should ignore it; RDF instance data does not need a Container node.</heritageGraph:design_note>
